Migrate the C native launcher peer to the r10 owned ring

The production native peer now negotiates shell r10. It fills ring slot 0
in place and offers it, consumes the Accepted ResourceStatus through the
native session, and waits for the exact SlotReleased. It then adopts the
settled offer with sophia_ns_adopt_image, which frees the slot. The
lifecycle assertions are unchanged.
